What was copied: KinematicCharacterController::move_shape and the private
functions it calls (check_and_fix_penetrations, snap_to_ground,
predict_ground, detect_grounded_status_and_apply_friction,
is_grounded_at_contact_manifold, handle_slopes, split_into_components,
compute_hit_info, decompose_hit, compute_dims, handle_stairs, subtract_hit),
the private structs HitInfo and HitDecomposition, and the body of the private
method CharacterLength::eval.

What si-rpg-engine changed, 2026-09-25 and 2026-09-26:

- One branch in decompose_hit (2026-09-25). When the hit normal crossed with
  the controller's up vector has no direction, the tangent's component along
  up is the vertical tangent and the rest is the horizontal tangent; Rapier
  files the whole tangent as vertical there. With a floor normal that is
  vertical but for its last bit, Rapier's routine then keeps none of a
  character's horizontal travel for that quantum. The report upstream is
  https://github.com/dimforge/rapier/issues/1019.
- A second cast in move_shape (2026-09-26). When the move's first cast finds
  nothing while the character was grounded at the start of the move, the
  routine casts once more with the skin (the controller's offset) 1e-9
  larger. A character standing on a floor starts its move with its skin on
  the floor's face to within rounding, and there parry's GJK cast can lose
  its search direction to rounding and report no hit, so the character takes
  its whole move, gravity step included, into its skin. The defect is
  parry's; the report upstream is https://github.com/dimforge/parry/issues/452.
- The routine is adapted to Rapier's public API: its methods live on a
  wrapper of KinematicCharacterController, a private method's body is a local
  function, and a crate-private field is read through its public accessor.
  The profiling attributes and the 2D branches are removed. Nothing else it
  computes is changed.

